Spec: Feature Issue 84 - HTTP 4xx as WARN and without Query String

Purpose:
  Log HTTP client errors of mitm_http-server as `WARN` instead of `ERROR` and never log query strings, so `system_logs` errors are real server errors and no OIDC codes or other query parameters are stored. Issue: https://github.com/Zheng-Bote/mitm_core-layer/issues/84

Platform: Rust/Linux

References:
  ../../../core-layer.sdd
  ../../../mitm_http-server/mitm_http-server.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Can modify:
  /mitm_http-server/src/main.rs
  /mitm_http-server/Cargo.toml
  /mitm_http-server/CHANGELOG.md
  /mitm_http-server/README.md

Must:
  An HTTP 5xx response is written as `HTTP <status> - <method> <path>` with level `ERROR` to system_logs and logged with `log::error!`.
  An HTTP 4xx response is written as `HTTP <status> - <method> <path>` with level `WARN` to system_logs and logged with `log::warn!`.
  Only the URI path is logged, never the query string.

Must not:
  Change other `log_system` calls, the response, or the API.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Derive level and message from status, method and path in `error_logging_middleware`.
  [x] #2 Unit tests for 4xx, 5xx and query-string stripping.
  [x] #3 Version 3.2.1, CHANGELOG.

Done when:
  `cargo build` and `cargo test` of mitm-http-server succeed.

Scenario: client error
  Given a request `GET /dashboard?x=1` is answered with HTTP 404
  Then system_logs contains `HTTP 404 Not Found - GET /dashboard` with level `WARN`

Scenario: failed OIDC callback
  Given `GET /api/v1/auth/oidc/callback?code=abc&state=xyz` is answered with HTTP 400
  Then neither system_logs nor STDOUT contain `abc` or `xyz`
